From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: do not leak reset_count on a failed recovery

A reset work that finds another reset in progress waits 20 s for it to
complete; when the wait times out it proceeds without dropping the
count of the reset it waited for, and a later success drops the count
only once. After any recovery that needed a retry, reset_count stays at
1, so every later crash first waits 20 s for a completion that never
comes and starts with fail_cont_count already raised.

Drop the failed reset's count when the wait times out. If that reset
completes after all (a round longer than 20 s), its success must not
take the count below 0, so the success paths use
atomic_dec_if_positive().
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1686,7 +1686,7 @@ static void ath12k_core_restart(struct w
 
 	if (ab->is_reset) {
 		if (!test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags)) {
-			atomic_dec(&ab->reset_count);
+			atomic_dec_if_positive(&ab->reset_count);
 			ab->is_reset = false;
 			atomic_set(&ab->fail_cont_count, 0);
 			clear_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags);
@@ -1931,6 +1931,14 @@ static void ath12k_core_reset(struct wor
 		ab->reset_fail_timeout = jiffies + ATH12K_RESET_FAIL_TIMEOUT_HZ;
 		/* Record the continuous recovery fail count when recovery failed*/
 		fail_cont_count = atomic_inc_return(&ab->fail_cont_count);
+
+		/*
+		 * The reset waited for failed and will never complete; stop
+		 * counting it. This run is now the only reset in progress, and
+		 * a later success drops reset_count back to 0. Otherwise every
+		 * later crash would first wait 20 s here for nothing.
+		 */
+		atomic_dec(&ab->reset_count);
 	}
 
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_BOOT, "reset starting\n");
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -13825,7 +13825,8 @@ ath12k_mac_op_reconfig_complete(struct i
 			 * the recovery has to be done for each radio
 			 */
 			if (recovery_count == ab->num_radios) {
-				atomic_dec(&ab->reset_count);
+				/* not below 0: see ath12k_core_reset() */
+				atomic_dec_if_positive(&ab->reset_count);
 				ab->is_reset = false;
 				atomic_set(&ab->fail_cont_count, 0);
 				clear_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags);
